    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "It all starts with light! Light bounces off everything around you, and some of it comes into your eyes.",
      "punch": "light",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "💡",
        "text": "Light bounces off things",
        "cue": "bounces",
        "sub": "Into your eyes!",
        "sub_cue": "eyes"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "How does it get in?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Through the black dot in the middle of your eye. It's called the pupil, and it's really a little hole!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "⚫",
        "text": "The pupil: a tiny hole",
        "cue": "pupil",
        "sub": "Lets the light in",
        "sub_cue": "hole"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What's the coloured part around it?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "That's the iris! It can be brown, blue, green or grey. It makes the pupil bigger in the dark and smaller in bright light.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "In the dark",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Pupil gets big",
              "icon": "🌑",
              "cue": "bigger"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "Bright light",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Pupil gets small",
              "icon": "☀️",
              "cue": "smaller"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Then what happens inside?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "A clear part called the lens focuses the light onto the back of your eye. And guess what? The picture lands upside down!",
      "punch": "upside",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "Inside your eye",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Lens focuses light",
            "icon": "🔍",
            "cue": "lens"
          },
          {
            "label": "Picture on the back",
            "icon": "🎯",
            "cue": "back"
          },
          {
            "label": "It's upside down!",
            "icon": "🙃",
            "cue": "upside"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Upside down? But I see everything the right way up!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "That's your brain's job! Your eye sends a message to your brain, and it flips the picture the right way up.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🧠",
        "text": "Your brain flips it!",
        "cue": "flips",
        "sub": "A message from the eye",
        "sub_cue": "message"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "One safety rule: never look straight at the Sun. It's much too bright and can hurt your eyes.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🚫",
        "text": "Never stare at the Sun",
        "cue": "never",
        "sub": "Too bright for eyes",
        "sub_cue": "bright"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So light comes in, the lens focuses it, and my brain flips the picture. Wow!",
      "board": {
